cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use prosediff in your work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: prosediff
abstract: >-
  A side-by-side diff for prose, not code. prosediff compares two versions of
  Word, OpenDocument and Markdown documents, from two files, two folders or a
  git repository: it pairs each paragraph and sentence with the one it came
  from, follows text that moved even when it was edited, highlights the
  changed words and formatting, and shows the comments added and removed. It
  writes an HTML report, unified and word diffs, or a copy of the new document
  with every change as a tracked change, so a version edited with Track
  Changes off gets them back. An AI (Claude, ChatGPT through Codex, a local
  model through Ollama, or any provider any-llm reaches) can assess the
  changes and mark the problems it finds in the text.
authors:
